<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Joseph Gabler</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1700–1771</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Joseph Gabler was a German organ builder from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ochsenhausen">Ochsenhausen</a> in upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/swabia">Swabia</a>. After building an organ for the abbey church of his home town, he created his most famous instrument, the great organ of Weingarten Abbey, completed in 1750 with more than 6,000 pipes. His organs are counted among the outstanding baroque instruments of southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>.</p></div>
